 # Unreleased changes
 
-- **Under review — 3D models: styles and the 3D model panel:** a molecule shown in 3D or Both gets a **Properties → 3D model** section with **Stick** (tubes with mitered joints and one outline round their outer edge), **Wireframe** and **Space-filling** (van der Waals radii) styles beside **Ball & stick**, each with a pictogram; a **Flat · journal** or **Glossy · slides** look; **All**, **Polar** or **None** hydrogens; **Depth fade** and **Perspective** sliders; a **None** or **Soft card** background; and **Reset view**. Model colours follow the drawing's colour theme and canvas (Publication uses Presentation's colours, with a light grey hydrogen); on a dark canvas the flat look's outline is a soft light rim and the soft card is dark. Each change is one Undo step, a slider drag included. The canvas now draws models with the PNG export renderer, so balls shade smoothly without rings at any zoom and each bond's shading runs on across its colour change. [3D models](3d-keyboard-drawing.md#show-a-molecule-as-a-3d-model) · [Issue #386](https://github.com/Ameyanagi/ReShiki/issues/386) · @Ameyanagi.
