-- **Under review — 3D models: rotate, resize and the Show-as bar:** once a shown model is selected, drag inside its frame to rotate it, **Shift**-drag to roll it and double-click to reset the view; corner handles resize the frame. An unselected model, or its frame's edge, still drags to move. A small **Show as 2D · 3D · Both** bar floats above a selected molecule and hides while you drag. Going back to 2D can keep the **Original drawing** or flatten the model **From the 3D view** as it is turned now, with far bonds lighter, like 3D optimize. When a model appears, its atoms move from the drawing into 3D and the hydrogens grow out. The **3D tilt** tool, its X/Y step commands and the **Tilt X / Tilt Y** fields turn a molecule shown only in 3D by turning its model and leave its hidden 2D drawing as it is; drawn objects selected with it tilt as before. The rotation handle, **Rotate 180°**, the rotate step keys and the **Rotate** field roll such a model about the view axis instead of turning its hidden drawing; a flip leaves it alone, since a mirrored model would be the other enantiomer. Each rotation, tilt, resize and flatten is one Undo step, and every drag commits exactly what it previews. [3D models](3d-keyboard-drawing.md#show-a-molecule-as-a-3d-model) · [Issue #386](https://github.com/Ameyanagi/ReShiki/issues/386) · @Ameyanagi.
