-- **Under review — 3D models of structures:** select a molecule and choose **2D**, **3D** or **Both** in the new **Properties → Structure** section to show it as a vector ball & stick model in place of its drawing or beside it, with the shading, outlines, depth fade and perspective of the approved prototype. The conformer comes from the 3D optimize worker (ETKDG, then MMFF94s) and is kept for switching back; each switch is one Undo step, and chemistry, atom IDs and the 2D layout never change. Clicking the model selects its molecule; a chemical edit removes the model. Flipping, resizing (except the model's own corner handles), cleaning up, optimizing or joining a molecule shown only in 3D asks you to switch to 2D, and rings never fuse onto its hidden bonds. `.rsk` files keep models, and PNG, SVG and PDF draw them. Every file is now saved as document version 28, so ReShiki 0.12.0 cannot open it. [3D models](3d-keyboard-drawing.md#show-a-molecule-as-a-3d-model) · [Issue #386](https://github.com/Ameyanagi/ReShiki/issues/386) · @Ameyanagi.
