-- **Under review — Attached marks orbit their atom:** dragging an attached lone pair, charge or radical, from the atom with a chemical symbol or by its handle, now moves it around the atom in 15° steps just outside the label, with the same gap a click uses all the way round, skipping steps that would touch a bond, while a dashed orbit and dots show the positions. Hold **Option/Alt** or **Shift** to place it freely. Lone pairs turn across the line from the atom in either case and turn with the molecule when it is rotated or flipped; charges stay upright. [Chemical symbols](scientific-symbols.md#add-a-mark-to-an-atom) · [Issue #387](https://github.com/Ameyanagi/ReShiki/issues/387) · @Ameyanagi.
